        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "The library's signature engine: direct FFI bindings to OpenSSL libcrypto for Bitcoin's ECDSA. Classical, broken by Shor — but secp256k1 ECDSA is fixed by Bitcoin consensus rules, so replacement with ML-DSA is a protocol-level decision, not changeable in this library alone (observable here, replaceable only by the Bitcoin protocol). The spec site exercises real signature validation."
